INSERT INTO `ha_term_relationships` (`object_id`,`term_taxonomy_id`,`term_order`) SELECT @translation_id,tt.term_taxonomy_id,0 FROM `ha_term_taxonomy` tt JOIN `ha_terms` t ON t.term_id=tt.term_id WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND tt.taxonomy='category' AND t.slug='iraq' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_term_relationships` r WHERE r.object_id=@translation_id AND r.term_taxonomy_id=tt.term_taxonomy_id) LIMIT 1;
INSERT INTO `ha_posts` (`post_author`,`post_date`,`post_date_gmt`,`post_content`,`post_title`,`post_excerpt`,`post_status`,`comment_status`,`ping_status`,`post_name`,`post_modified`,`post_modified_gmt`,`post_parent`,`guid`,`menu_order`,`post_type`,`post_mime_type`,`comment_count`) SELECT 1,NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),'<h2>Why is choosing a 90 mm pipe critical in modern irrigation?</h2><p>In subterranean and surface irrigation systems, selecting the appropriate diameter for the main line directly affects pressure loss, costs, and irrigation efficiency. The 90 mm pipe with internal and external threading is a popular option for medium to large farms due to its high mechanical strength and safety against accidental connection failures. These pipes are typically used to transfer water from the main reservoir to lateral lines in drip and tape systems. Ensuring the proper installation of these pipes not only prevents leaks but also prevents additional stress on the pump and pressure-regulating equipment. If you are designing a new system, reading the <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D8%A8%D8%B0%D8%B1-%D8%AA%D8%B1%DB%8C%D8%AA%DB%8C%DA%A9%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%87-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Triticale seed rate per hectare</a> can be helpful to also consider the plant delivery variables, as the output flow of the emitters must be proportional to the transfer capacity of the main pipe.</p><h2>Equipment and tools required for installing 90 mm threaded pipe</h2><p>Before starting the installation process, ensuring the completeness of the required equipment list prevents field problems. This process cannot be performed without appropriate tools and quality fittings.</p><ul><li><strong>90 mm polyethylene (PE) pipe:</strong> Preferably meeting irrigation standards and UV-resistant.</li><li><strong>90-thread couplings and branch fittings:</strong> Homogeneous with the main pipe to prevent chemical incompatibility.</li><li><strong>Band fittings and O-ring seals:</strong> For pressurized connections requiring a full grip.</li><li><strong>Wrench and sharp utility knife:</strong> For clean, angled pipe cuts.</li><li><strong>Sealant or polymer adhesive:</strong> Depends on the type of fitting selected (coupling or band).</li></ul><h3>Key considerations when selecting fittings</h3><p>The use of mismatched fittings can lead to hidden leaks. It is recommended to use a single reputable brand for all main connections. In tape systems with higher operating pressures, the use of rims and filters before the 90-millimeter pipe inlet is mandatory to prevent system clogging. Familiarization with <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/%D9%85%DB%8C%D8%B2%D8%A7%D9%86-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%B4%D8%AA-%D9%84%D9%88%D8%A8%DB%8C%D8%A7-%DA%86%DB%8C%D8%AA%DB%8C-%D8%AF%D8%B1-%D9%87%DA%A9%D8%AA%D8%A7%D8%B1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cowpea yield per hectare</a> This indicates that the irrigation system must have sufficient flexibility to supply various crops throughout the year; therefore, the main pipe design must be able to manage different flows without critical pressure drop.</p><h2>Operational stages for installing 90-millimeter pipe</h2><p>Proper installation execution requires adherence to a logical sequence of operations. Negligence at any stage can jeopardize the entire project.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مراحل-نصب-لوله-نخ-دار-90-میلیمتر-در-سیستم-آبیاری-تصویر-شاخص.webp" alt="مراحل نصب لوله نخ دار 90 میلیمتر در سیستم آبیاری - تصویر 1"/><figcaption>product installation drip system 90-millimeter threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><ol><li><strong>Path reverse engineering:</strong> Before cutting, mark the final path of the main line on the ground from the reservoir to the first branch. The pipe slope should follow the ground contour to facilitate air venting. Downhill sections require dowel vents to collect air.</li><li><strong>Precise pipe cutting:</strong> Use a hacksaw or a dedicated pipe cutter to cut the pipe squarely, ensuring it is perfectly perpendicular to the longitudinal axis. A slanted cut prevents the O-ring seal from seating fully, leading to leaks.</li><li><strong>Deburring and cleaning:</strong> Clean the interior of the pipe of all grease, dust, and cutting chips. Any suspended particle may become lodged in the tip tape strip.</li><li><strong>Installing couplings:</strong> Position the pipe at the joint so the internal gasket is seated. Secure the connection by tightening the metal or plastic band over the pipe\'s spigot. Ensure the tightening torque does not deform the band.</li><li><strong>Installing branches (Tees and Elbows):</strong> Use appropriate branch connectors to connect drip or tape lines to the 90mm main line. Adjust the spacing between branches to match the outlet flow rate of each line so that pressure loss at the end of the lines remains within acceptable limits.</li></ol><h3>Safety notes and pipe support</h3><p>A 90mm pipe under water pressure has significant weight. In open areas, use plastic or wooden supports every 3 to 4 meters to prevent the pipe from contacting the ground or sharp stones. On steep slopes, use cleats to prevent longitudinal pipe stretching. If your system includes moisture-sensitive crops such as spinach, precise control of branch flow rates through valves is critical to prevent root waterlogging.</p><h2>Pressure testing and system troubleshooting after installation</h2><p>After connecting all drip or tape lines to the 90mm main line, test the system in a closed state (with an end cap on the line). Start the pump and gradually increase the pressure to the system\'s maximum rated value (typically 3 to 5 bar for this type of pipe).</p><ul><li><strong>Leak check:</strong> As water flows, feel all coupling connections and branches with your hand. The smallest water seep indicates the need to reopen the connection.</li><li><strong>Air test:</strong> With the air vents open, ensure the water flows smoothly and without bubbles. Air pockets in the system cause pipe vibration and fitting corrosion.</li><li><strong>Flow stability:</strong> Measure the flow rate at the end of the lines furthest from the source, where flow is laminar. If the pressure drop exceeds 15 percent of the nominal nozzle values, optimize the route or increase the diameter.</li></ul><p>Study <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/fasoolia-yield-per-hectare-iraq/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bean yield per hectare</a> This indicates crop dependency on regular irrigation continuity; therefore, resolving initial installation defects directly affects the farm\'s economic performance. The 90 millimeter pipe can withstand high flow rates, but when used for filter flushing, it is necessary to prevent impurities from returning to the main reservoir.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مراحل-نصب-لوله-نخ-دار-90-میلیمتر-در-سیستم-آبیاری-کاربرد-عملی.webp" alt="مراحل نصب لوله نخ دار 90 میلیمتر در سیستم آبیاری - تصویر 2"/><figcaption>product installation drip system 90 millimeter threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><h2>Frequently asked questions about 90 threaded pipe installation</h2><h3>Is it possible to use a 90 mm pipe for 16 mm drip lines?</h3><p>Yes, a 90 mm pipe is used as the main line to supply multiple drip lines. However, the number of branch connections must be controlled so that the pressure drop at the end of the drip lines does not exceed the acceptable limit (usually 20%). The use of flow control valves at branch points is also recommended.</p><h3>What is the appropriate support spacing for a 90 mm pipe on straight paths?</h3><p>On straight paths with minimal slope, place supports every 3 to 4 meters. In sloped areas or where the line crosses natural obstacles, reduce the spacing to 1.5 meters. Ensuring the pipe is not overly taut allows it to expand freely due to summer heat without subjecting fittings to tensile stress.</p><h3>Can a 90 mm pipe be combined with 63 mm or 125 mm pipes?</h3><p>Combining different pipe diameters using a ditch or reducing connectors is possible. However, in a standard drip system, it is best to avoid frequent diameter changes to keep the pressure drop predictable. If diameter changes are necessary, precise hydraulic calculations must be performed for these specific combinations.</p>\n<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><img src="https://navar-abyari.ir/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/navar-article-generated/مراحل-نصب-لوله-نخ-دار-90-میلیمتر-در-سیستم-آبیاری-جزئیات-فنی.webp" alt="مراحل نصب لوله نخ دار 90 میلیمتر در سیستم آبیاری - تصویر 3"/><figcaption>product installation drip system 90 millimeter threaded pipe</figcaption></figure><p>To optimize twin or intercropped planting, understanding the relationship between irrigation flow rate and total crop yield is key. For example, in crops such as oblong watermelon, precise management of the outlet pressure from the 90 mm main line can increase fruit volume and quality. Therefore, accurate installation and initial system testing are a direct investment in reducing waste and increasing yield in future seasons.</p><h2>Conclusion: Strategies for Success in Irrigation Projects</h2><p>Installing 90 mm threaded pipe is a critical technical step in deploying drip and tape irrigation systems. By adhering to proper cutting principles, using standard fittings, ensuring adequate support, and conducting complete pressure testing, you can prevent costly repairs and system performance degradation during the mid-season irrigation period. Attention to minor details, such as slope for air venting and pipe cleanliness, distinguishes an efficient system from a defective one. With proper planning and adherence to the guidelines provided in this article, you can maximize your investment in irrigation infrastructure and lay the foundation for sustainable crop growth.</p>\n<p><strong>Related articles:</strong> <a href="https://navar-abyari.ir/eggplant-seed-quantity-per-hectare-planting-irrigation-tips/">eggplant seed quantity per hectare planting irrigation tips</a></p>','Comprehensive Guide to Installing 90 mm Threaded Tubing in Drip and Tape Irrigation Systems','90 threaded pipes are the backbone of many pressurized irrigation systems. This guide covers the correct installation process, common errors, and safety tips for optimal performance of drip and tape systems.','publish','closed','closed','90-mm-threaded-tubing-installation-drip-tape-irrigation-guide',NOW(),UTC_TIMESTAMP(),0,'',0,'post','',0 WHERE @source_post_id IS NOT NULL AND @translation_id IS NULL AND @slug_conflict IS NULL;
INSERT INTO `ha_postmeta` (`post_id`,`meta_key`,`meta_value`) SELECT @translation_id,'_navar_translation_queue_key','article-translation:prod-039:en-US' WHERE @translation_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `ha_postmeta` WHERE post_id=@translation_id AND meta_key='_navar_translation_queue_key');
